bic_trace_step.reason:
The diff shows that __arm_lpae_unmap (which returns size_t, an unsigned type) is changed from returning 0 to returning -ENOENT when !pte. Specifically, the code changes:
- if (WARN_ON(!pte))
-    return 0;
+ if (!pte) {
+    WARN_ON(!(data->iop.cfg.quirks & IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_NO_WARN));
+    return -ENOENT;
+ }
and similarly in the loop: originally WARN_ON(!pte) with a break, now returns -ENOENT. Returning a negative error code from a size_t function causes unsigned wraparound to a huge value, which matches the described root cause. This commit introduces the vulnerable construct; it does not contain any fix for it.
